          "caption": "A9 Drumochter Pass A single carriageway section of the infamous A9 road linking Inverness with the South. Usually it is not as quiet as this, taking such a photo would involve being mown down by a caravan and the thirty odd vehicles stuck behind it.\nDruim Uachdair itself is the range of hills (left) to the west of the pass.\n\nPhoto taken at c.450m asl, normally there is a lot more snow about, and a few days  earlier I had a very difficult crossing when the road was not gritted.",
